       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **You aren't a prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst. The confirmation I asked for had to come from the treating clinician, and it didn't.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum for adults. A confirmation doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n\nHere is what you can do:\n1. Ask the treating prescriber to review the intended dose. If it was meant to be 400 mg or 800 mg per dose, they can enter or correct it.\n2. If the prescriber really intends this dose, they should enter it themselves. Pharmacy will review it and may contact them about it.\n\nOnce a prescriber gives me a dose within the standard range, I can enter that order for you."
